# Frontend (Vite) — safe to expose in the browser bundle.
# Copy this file to .env and fill in real values for local development.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
# VITE_SITE_URL=https://food.saovia.net   # optional override, see src/lib/seo.ts

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Everything below is SERVER-SIDE ONLY. None of it belongs in this file, in
# any .env* file, in a frontend component, in localStorage, or in git.
#
#   - Set once per project, as Supabase Edge Function secrets:
#       supabase secrets set RESEND_API_KEY=...
#       supabase secrets set SMTP_FROM_EMAIL=noreply@saovia.net
#       supabase secrets set SMTP_FROM_NAME="SAOVIA FOOD"
#     Read only by supabase/functions/_shared/email/config.ts (Deno edge
#     runtime) — never imported by anything under src/.
#
#   - Supabase Auth's own Custom SMTP (Dashboard → Project Settings →
#     Auth → SMTP Settings, or supabase/config.toml's [auth.email.smtp]
#     pushed via `supabase config push`) needs its own 4 values, entered
#     directly there — again never in a repo .env file:
#       SMTP_HOST      = smtp.resend.com
#       SMTP_PORT      = 587
#       SMTP_USER      = resend
#       SMTP_PASSWORD  = <the same Resend API key as RESEND_API_KEY above>
#     (config.toml reads these via env(SMTP_HOST) etc. at `config push`
#     time from your shell/CI environment, still never committed.)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
